# Use with VS Code REST Client or Visual Studio (.http). Start the API first: dotnet run --project src/AiOralExam.Api
@host = http://localhost:5080

# Sign-in happens in Keycloak (password grant is disabled), so get a token through Swagger:
# http://localhost:5080/swagger -> Authorize -> sign in as han.hg@aives.edu.vn / Password@123,
# run any request and copy the token from the "Authorization: Bearer ..." header of the shown curl command.
# Tokens expire after 5 minutes.
@token = paste-access-token-here

### My exam sessions
GET {{host}}/api/interview/my-sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update my profile (own account)
PATCH {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Updated Full Name" }

### Start an attempt (SWD392 session, currently open)
POST {{host}}/api/interview-attempts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "examSessionId": "33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" }

### Submit an answer (replace ATTEMPT_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/interview-attempts/ATTEMPT_ID/responses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "answerText": "A modular monolith is deployed as one unit but split into business modules; each module owns its tables and talks to the others only through interfaces." }

### Health check
GET {{host}}/health

### Create a user (administrator)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Han Hoang Giang",
  "email": "new.student@aives.edu.vn",
  "role": "Student",
  "studentCode": "SE180099",
  "lecturerCode": null
}

### Resend a user's password setup email (administrator; replace USER_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users/USER_ID/setup-link
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
